  "title": "SeeTraceAct: Visibility-Aware Latent Planning from Cross-Embodiment Demonstration Videos",
  "title_zh": "SeeTraceAct：从跨具身示范视频进行可见性感知潜规划",
  "abstract": "Vision-language-action models (VLAs) are promising general-purpose robot policies, but adapting them to new tasks typically requires costly task-specific teleoperation data. As an alternative, we study one-shot demo-conditioned VLAs, where a robot policy is conditioned on a single demonstration video of an unseen task. We find that existing end-to-end approaches often struggle when successful execution requires precisely localizing small target regions. To address this limitation, we propose See",
